KG42.register("slice-clusters-3d5157310e5888a4dba43482",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v142-d-CL002","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","title":"Demand-bid aggregation, ISO clearing, and microgrid share allocation","source_pointer":"/clusters/134","node_ids":["COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999","COMP-c1310ff0c42d5a65","COMP-ebacec241379c91d"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R002","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R004","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R005"],"visible_rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R002","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R004","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R005"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-6123cc742177db42","source":"KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999","target":"COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","type":"links","assertion_ids":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-3a1e92203c1201ed","source":"COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","target":"COMP-c1310ff0c42d5a65","type":"limits","assertion_ids":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-52149ac6e45479fc","source":"COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","target":"COMP-c1310ff0c42d5a65","type":"links","assertion_ids":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E002"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-e75e496d6aa75231","source":"KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999","target":"COMP-c1310ff0c42d5a65","type":"links","assertion_ids":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E003"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-4632ebe6f79f5ca6","source":"COMP-ebacec241379c91d","target":"COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","type":"conditional_on","assertion_ids":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R004"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-ad0861614c9d7f4a","source":"COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","target":"KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999","type":"links","assertion_ids":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"],"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R005"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e037"],"rationale":"The source explicitly describes receiving bids from microgrids and from optional responsive loads, merging the bids, and submitting them to the ISO as associated responsibilities. This supports the functional linkage between reception and aggregation and does not add a C-graph edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e037","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The aggregated demand bids sent by the DMO are the source of the demand bids received by the ISO. The social-welfare branch remains conditional on the ISO considering demand bids. A mathematical identity from the bid curve to the benefit function has not been established on this basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-D-bt","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-D","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that the ISO award result enters DMO disaggregation, so D_{bt} at both ends is retained as a quantity interface pending verification. The correspondence between bus b and the DMO service domain is not yet clear. This connection does not treat the two objects as already equal in quantity, and it does not directly rewrite total ISO demand as the awarded quantity of a single DMO."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g01-e037"],"rationale":"The same set of microgrid bids both participates in aggregation and serves as the basis for local disaggregation after the award. This supports reuse of bid information. Bid monotonicity cannot directly replace the segment feasible region or the definition of the objective coefficients."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-df-mt","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-df","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e031","v141-b-g01-e032","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E18"],"rationale":"The fixed non-responsive load in the bids enters the aggregation accounting and the award accounting of each microgrid, and the conditions that it cannot be changed under normal operation and must be fully supplied are retained. The parameter objects of the two stages are retained separately."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
